[1m== GROWTH 6. The half this seed CANNOT reach, and exactly what is missing because of it[0m
   A capture is not a consent. The grant is written by POST /v1/growth/subscription-confirmations, which
   takes the single-use token from the confirmation email -- and that token exists in exactly one place:
   the guest's mailbox. Only its SHA-256 hash is persisted, so it cannot be recovered from the API, and
   the bound provider (GrowthFakeMailProvider) is an in-process per-request recorder that performs no
   network I/O and exposes no endpoint. There is no mailbox on this machine to open and no route that
   reveals the token.
   
   So this seed produces NONE of the following, and does not pretend otherwise:
     * no NEW consented contact (no confirm -> no consent receipt -> not a segment candidate)
     * no withdrawal and no suppression (the one-click credential is minted by a dispatch and mailed;
       same problem, and GROWTH's own rule is that a suppression must be the guest's act)
     * no delivery and no dispatch run (see the header: sending is the human's walk, not the seed's)
   The consented contacts counted in step 4 were granted by earlier confirmations in this world.

